# Executive PDF reports (always)

**Canonical style:** Goal SIP (Standard vs Step-Up) and MF vs FD HTML dossiers. Every new or updated calculator PDF must match that look. Do **not** invent a new report layout or default to plain `generateCalculatorReport` jsPDF when shipping a client-facing report.

## Stack (required)

| Piece | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Sheet shell | `src/components/reports/executive-dossier.tsx` (`ExecutiveDossierSheet`, headings, playbook) |
| Composition donuts | `src/components/reports/report-composition-donut.tsx` |
| Capture | `generatePdfFromElement` in `src/lib/pdf-generator.ts` |
| Reference dossiers | `goal-sip-dossier.tsx`, `mf-vs-fd-dossier.tsx` |

Pattern: mount an off-screen `*Dossier` with live calc data → Download calls `generatePdfFromElement(REPORT_ID, filename)`.

`generateCalculatorReport` (raw jsPDF) is legacy only until that calculator gets an HTML dossier. Do not use it for new client reports.

## Visual system (do not freestyle)

- White **900px** sheet, Finoptic logo, emerald brand line, uppercase black title
- Header meta card: client name, context fields, **email + phone** (use `DUMMY_REPORT_CONTACT` until CRM)
- Dual comparison cards when comparing two paths (dark slate vs emerald accent). No winner badges like "Preferred" / "Higher Return" / "Lower Return"
- Assumptions grid, `ReportCompositionDonut` (invested / gain / tax + %), schedule table (slate header, emerald milestone rows), `ExecutivePlaybook`, disclaimer + "Powered by Nivra"
- Rose "friction / notes / delay" panels when the page has warnings or cost-of-delay
- Mark blocks that must not slice across pages with `data-pdf-keep-together`

## Client-facing copy (hard)

- **Never** put internal Excel paths or workbook names in the PDF (no `Unprotected…`, no `v1.xlsm`, no Full Set filenames)
- **No em dashes (—) or en dashes (–)** in report copy; use periods, commas, or "to"
- Do not label vehicles "Preferred" / "Recommended" / "Higher Return" / "Lower Return" on primary milestone cards
- Money: full INR via `formatINRCurrency` (not compact L/Cr)
- Percents: human form via `formatPercent`

## Checklist when adding a calculator report

1. Clone structure from `mf-vs-fd-dossier.tsx` or `goal-sip-dossier.tsx`
2. Map every important page output (stats, mixes, insights, notes, schedule) into dossier sections
3. Pass `contact` (or rely on dummy defaults on the sheet)
4. Wire Download → `generatePdfFromElement` + loading spinner (see `mf-vs-fd.tsx` / `goal-sip-planner.tsx`)
5. Playbook from `report-playbooks.ts` (client-safe wording only)
6. Spot-check PDF: no internal filenames, no em dashes, email/phone present, notes block not cut across pages
